From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:10:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw a renderer's backdrop on its own clock, and hook
 embedders in before paint

The shell asks the renderer when its backdrop next needs a frame
(`backdrop_frame_due`) and presents it from `about_to_wait`
(`render_backdrop`), without resolving, laying out or painting the
document. Nothing is scheduled while the window is occluded, hidden or
minimised, or while nothing visible moves.

`WindowConfig::with_before_paint` runs an embedder's hook after the
document is resolved and before each frame is painted, with the renderer
and the animation clock: where an embedder keeps renderer state, such as
the backdrop, in step with the document.

dioxus-native's renderers forward the backdrop; vello_cpu draws none.
`RendererOptions::allow_software_gpu` lets the gpu-cpu-fallback renderer
draw through wgpu on a software adapter, to test the GPU path without a
GPU.
